The AV1 range writer in lib/src/av1/range_encoder.dart is based on the
go-av1 od_ec range encoder (cf2eb172dac31e754243a1c6b756991e229dc1ff).
See licenses/go-av1.txt for the BSD 2-Clause terms.

The default CDFs used by the AV1 palette writer are defined by the Alliance
for Open Media AV1 Bitstream & Decoding Process Specification, section 10.2.

The H.264 CABAC intra decoder is based on Eyevinn hi264
(76f3e392076aaf47faf64e3f0d0904115494e2b1). See licenses/hi264.txt for
the MIT terms. The probability and scan tables are defined by ITU-T H.264.

The H.264 inter macroblock parser and CAVLC tables use Rui Carmo's go-264
as a reference (cecca3835cbdf52167c9d892caacfa8eda6eb406). See
licenses/go-264.txt for the MIT terms.
